      "body": "\n\n## Overview\n\nFix macOS path canonicalization and `/tmp` directory cleanup in `docker/entrypoints/test_vllm_nonroot_entrypoint.sh` (used by the `test-nonroot-entrypoint` pre-commit hook) and replace Bash 4+ `${hardware,,}` syntax in `tools/recipes/serve_with_recipe.sh` with POSIX `tr` so both scripts run cleanly on macOS.\n\n## Claims\n\n- Canonicalizes `WORKDIR=\"$(cd \"$(mktemp -d)\" && pwd -P)\"` in `docker/entrypoints/test_vllm_nonroot_entrypoint.sh` so `case8`–`case10` pass on macOS where `/var` is a symlink to `/private/var`.\n- Tracks and cleans up `/tmp/vllm-home.*` fallback directories created by `case2` and `case3` in `docker/entrypoints/test_vllm_nonroot_entrypoint.sh`.\n- Replaces Bash 4+ `${hardware,,}` case-conversion parameter expansion in `tools/recipes/serve_with_recipe.sh` with `printf '%s' \"$hardware\" | tr '[:upper:]' '[:lower:]'` so the script runs under macOS `/bin/bash` (Bash 3.2).\n\n## Validation\n\n- **Reproducer (without fix vs with fix):**\n  - Without fix on macOS: `sh docker/entrypoints/test_vllm_nonroot_entrypoint.sh` fails at `case8` (`FAIL: case8: symlink to existing dir -> resolved target (got '/private/var/folders/...', want '/var/folders/...')`), and `/bin/bash tools/recipes/serve_with_recipe.sh` fails with `${hardware,,}: bad substitution` when `--hardware` is passed.\n  - With fix: All 11 test cases in `test_vllm_nonroot_entrypoint.sh` pass (`ALL CASES PASSED.`) with zero leaked `/tmp/vllm-home.*` directories, and `serve_with_recipe.sh` lowercases `--hardware` under Bash 3.2.\n- **Test commands run:**\n  ```bash\n  sh docker/entrypoints/test_vllm_nonroot_entrypoint.sh\n  .venv/bin/pre-commit run --files docker/entrypoints/test_vllm_nonroot_entrypoint.sh tools/recipes/serve_with_recipe.sh\n  ```\n- **Results:** `ALL CASES PASSED.` (11/11 cases); `shellcheck` and `test-nonroot-entrypoint` pre-commit hooks passed.\n- **Model evaluation:** N/A (entrypoint test script and recipe launcher shell portability only).\n\n## Details\n\n- **Root cause:**\n  1. `vllm-nonroot-entrypoint.sh` resolves directory targets using `cd -P ... && pwd` (returning `/private/var/folders/...` on macOS), whereas `mktemp -d` in `test_vllm_nonroot_entrypoint.sh` returned `/var/folders/...` without `-P`. In addition, `case2` and `case3` triggered the entrypoint's `mktemp -d /tmp/vllm-home.XXXXXX` fallback without recording those paths for the `EXIT` trap cleanup.\n  2. `${var,,}` was introduced in Bash 4.0 and fails with `bad substitution` under `/bin/bash` on macOS (Bash 3.2).\n- **Duplicate-PR check:** Searched open PRs via `gh pr list --repo vllm-project/vllm --state open --search \"test_vllm_nonroot_entrypoint.sh OR serve_with_recipe.sh\"`; no open PR touches either file.\n- **AI assistance:** AI assistance was used to identify and verify these portability fixes and prepare this PR; all changes were reviewed and verified locally.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n\n",
